.TH XD\-RUN 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-run \- the Run dialog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-run
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-run
is the Run dialog of the Start menu: type the name of a program, folder,
document or Internet address, and it opens it.
A command line runs if its program is in
.B PATH
or given by its path
.RB ( ~
is the home folder); folders, documents and addresses open with their
default applications, through
.BR xdg\-open (1).
A name nothing in
.B PATH
answers can be a program's Windows name, as Windows' App Paths has it:
.B msconfig
(or
.BR msconfig.exe ,
in any case) starts the program whose desktop entry lists it in
.BR X\-XeonDesktop\-AppPath .
Browse... picks a file.
.PP
It remembers the last 26 commands; the last one is pre-filled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-style " style"
.TQ
.BI \-\-scheme " file"
The visual style and colour scheme instead of those in
.IR desktop.ini .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/xeondesktop/run\-history
The commands run, newest first (default
.IR ~/.local/state/xeondesktop/run\-history ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR xd\-choose\-file (1)
